UPDATE 2026-09-05 (seat06): PRIOR HYPOTHESIS REFUTED WITH DIRECT EVIDENCE -- "next inside line?{} doesn't
restart enclosing while loop" (2026-08-30/09-03 note) is WRONG: SCRIP's output and .expected are the exact
same 62-line multiset (verified via `sort`+`diff`, exit 0), only reordered -- a hypothesis predicting
missing/duplicated entries cannot explain a pure permutation of identical lines.
REAL MECHANISM, confirmed this session by instrumenting a SCRATCH COPY of the upstream twin
(corpus/packages/icon/jcon_tests/profsum.icn, not the checked-in test) to dump `!ptab`'s iteration order
right before the `sortf(l, 5)` call: real icont and SCRIP produce the IDENTICAL 61-element multiset of
table entries but in COMPLETELY DIFFERENT iteration order (verified side by side, not inferred -- see
LEDGER). Icon `!table` order depends on each implementation's own internal hashing, which is well-
established Icon knowledge but NOT independently re-confirmed against a written spec this session (searched
refs/icon-master's doc/ tree and found no explicit statement either way -- flagging the gap rather than
asserting more than was checked). A subsequent `sortf()` on a tied field is CONFIRMED STABLE AND CORRECT
against real icont (isolated 5-element record witness, ties preserve relative order identically on both
sides) -- so both the table contents and the sort are right on both sides; only the pre-sort order (an
implementation's own hash layout, not a language-guaranteed property) differs, and a stable sort preserves
whichever pre-sort order it was given.
